Scaly -- an expression shows its value, let x ... keeps one. :help
scaly> it: int = 3
scaly> x: int = 40
scaly> it: int = 42
scaly> n: int = 1
scaly> scaly> it: int = 10
scaly> scaly> p: Point
scaly> it: int = 25
scaly> xs: Array[int]
scaly>   ...>   ...>   ...> scaly> it: int = 16
scaly>   ...> scaly> it: int = 80
scaly> s: String = "Hallo 3"
scaly> it: String = "Hallo 3"
scaly> it: f64 = 0.30000000000000004
scaly> x + nope
    ^ unknown identifier: nope
scaly> done
scaly>   x: int
  n: int
  p: Point
  xs: Array[int]
  s: String
  it: f64
scaly>   x: int
    the value   8 bytes, on the session page of its entry
scaly>   s: String
    the value   8 bytes, on the session page of its entry
    its text    7 bytes, on the frame page of its entry
scaly>   xs: Array[int]
    the value   24 bytes, on the session page of its entry
    its buffer  5 of 8 elements, on the session page of its entry
scaly>   no value nope -- :values
scaly> big: Array[int]
scaly>   ...>   ...>   ...> scaly>   big: Array[int]
    the value   24 bytes, on the session page of its entry
    its buffer  1000 of 1014 elements, on a page of its own
scaly> ys: Array[int]
scaly>   ys: Array[int]
    the value   24 bytes, on the session page of its entry
    its buffer  none yet
